{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7336984","formula":"C₁₀H₁₄N₂","hill":"C10H14N2","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":14.0,"N":2.0},"names":{"en":"Rivanicline"},"descriptions":{"en":"Rivanicline (TC-2403, RJR-2403, (E)-metanicotine) is a drug which acts as a partial agonist at neural nicotinic acetylcholine receptors. It is subtype-selective, binding primarily to the α4β2 subtype. It has nootropic effects and was originally developed as a potential treatment for Alzheimer's disease, but a second action that was subsequently found was that it inhibits the production of Interleukin-8 and thus produces an antiinflammatory effect, and so it has also been developed as a potential treatment for ulcerative colitis."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":5310967,"mass":162.23,"charge":0,"smiles":"CNCC/C=C/C1=CN=CC=C1","inchikey":"JUOSGGQXEBBCJB-GORDUTHDSA-N","iupac":"(E)-N-methyl-4-pyridin-3-ylbut-3-en-1-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5310967","atoms":26,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-4.65,"y":0.208,"z":0.008,"el":"N"},{"x":3.046,"y":-1.487,"z":-0.149,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.33,"y":0.661,"z":-0.639,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.289,"y":-0.313,"z":0.043,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.92,"y":0.144,"z":-0.605,"el":"C"},{"x":0.089,"y":0.789,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":1.486,"y":0.326,"z":0.048,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.571,"y":-0.697,"z":0.681,"el":"C"},{"x":2.506,"y":1.216,"z":0.318,"el":"C"},{"x":1.787,"y":-0.997,"z":-0.177,"el":"C"},{"x":3.815,"y":0.749,"z":0.355,"el":"C"},{"x":4.03,"y":-0.599,"z":0.117,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.62,"y":0.802,"z":-1.688,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.394,"y":1.645,"z":-0.158,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.245,"y":-1.288,"z":-0.459,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.974,"y":-0.46,"z":1.084,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.756,"y":-0.788,"z":-1.138,"el":"H"},{"x":-4.944,"y":0.333,"z":-0.961,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.109,"y":1.737,"z"